Hello Thomas,
I tried to get a full backtrace using GDB, but unfortunately, the stack
trace cuts off at frame #4 (__GI_abort). I couldn't download the debug
symbols because the debuginfod server (debuginfod.neon.kde.org) kept timing
out on my end.
However, I did find the exact trigger for the crash:
The crash (ASSERT: "it != m_formatsIdToIndex.end()" in
katehighlight.cpp:181) happens specifically when I send commands from the
script editor to the R console.

"
[Detaching after vfork from child process 7710]
[Detaching after vfork from child process 7712]
ASSERT: "it != m_formatsIdToIndex.end()" in file
/workspace/build/src/syntax/katehighlight.c
pp, line 181
"



The application opens just fine, but the exact moment I execute a line of
code from the script editor into the console, it aborts.
Since the R console and script editor both use KTextEditor, it seems the
syntax engine is failing to look up a text format ID when passing the text
over. I hope this helps narrow it down!

Regards
Alfonso

